---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { localizedPath } from '../../i18n/utils';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const strings = t(locale);
---

<Legal
  locale={locale}
  routeKey="terms"
  title={strings.meta.termsTitle}
  description={strings.meta.termsDescription}
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) govern access to and use of the website{' '}
    <strong>{site.url.replace('https://', '')}</strong> (the “Site”), as well as the relationship
    between {site.legalName} and the people who visit it or contact us through it.
  </p>
  <p>
    By accessing the Site you confirm that you have read, understood and accepted these Terms. If
    you do not agree with them, please refrain from using the Site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="owner">1. Owner identification</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Legal name:</strong> {site.legalName}</li>
    <li><strong>Tax ID (RUC):</strong> {site.taxId}</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Registered address:</strong> {site.address.street}, {site.address.district},{' '}
      {site.address.city}, {site.address.country}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact email:</strong>{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email.legal}`}>{site.email.legal}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="purpose">2. Purpose and scope</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is informational and institutional in nature. It describes the technology consulting
    services offered by {site.shortName} and provides a contact channel.
  </p>
  <p>
    The content of the Site <strong>does not constitute a binding offer</strong> nor professional
    advice applicable to any specific case. The actual delivery of any service is governed by the
    contract, proposal or services agreement signed separately between {site.legalName} and the
    client. In the event of a conflict between these Terms and that contract, the contract prevails
    with respect to the contracted services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">3. Conditions of use</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to use the Site in accordance with the law, good faith and these Terms. In
    particular, you agree not to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the Site for unlawful or fraudulent purposes, or in ways that harm third-party rights.</li>
    <li>
      Introduce or distribute malicious software, or carry out actions that damage, overload or
      impair the Site or prevent its normal use by others.
    </li>
    <li>
      Attempt to gain unauthorised access to restricted areas, systems or networks connected to the
      Site, or circumvent its security measures.
    </li>
    <li>
      Systematically extract the Site’s content by automated means for commercial purposes without
      our prior written authorisation.
    </li>
    <li>Impersonate {site.shortName} or any other individual or legal entity.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ip">4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, graphics, logos, source code and other elements of the Site are owned by{' '}
    {site.legalName} or by third parties who have authorised their use, and are protected by
    Peruvian and international copyright and industrial property law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Viewing and reproducing extracts of the content for personal, non-commercial use is permitted
    provided the source is cited. Any other use — reproduction, distribution, public communication
    or transformation — requires prior written authorisation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">5. Third-party links and content</h2>
  <p>
    The Site may include links to third-party sites, offered for reference only. {site.shortName}{' '}
    does not control those sites and accepts no responsibility for their content, privacy policies
    or practices. You access them at your own risk.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party trademarks mentioned on the Site — including Microsoft, Power BI, Microsoft 365,
    Azure and Microsoft Entra ID — belong to their respective owners and are cited for descriptive
    purposes only. Their mention does not imply sponsorship, affiliation or endorsement by those
    owners unless expressly stated.
  </p>

  <h2 id="apps">6. Integrated applications and services</h2>
  <p>
    {site.shortName} may develop and register applications that integrate with third-party
    platforms, including Microsoft Entra ID. Where one of our applications requests permissions to
    access your organisation’s data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Access is strictly limited to the permissions expressly granted by you or by your
      organisation’s administrator during the consent process.
    </li>
    <li>
      Data is processed solely for the purposes described at the time of consent and in the
      corresponding services agreement.
    </li>
    <li>
      The processing of personal data is governed by our{' '}
      <a href={localizedPath('privacy', locale)}>Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You or your organisation’s administrator may revoke consent at any time from the
      administration console of the relevant platform.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="availability">7. Site availability</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep the Site continuously available, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or
    error-free operation. {site.shortName} may suspend, modify or discontinue access to the Site,
    in whole or in part, for maintenance, security or reasons beyond its control, without this
    giving rise to any right to compensation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The content of the Site is provided “as is”, without warranties of any kind as to its accuracy,
    currency or fitness for a particular purpose.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by Peruvian law, {site.legalName} shall not be liable for
    indirect damages, loss of profits or loss of data arising from access to or use of the Site,
    nor for decisions you make relying solely on the information published here.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that, under Peruvian law, cannot be
    excluded or limited — in particular liability arising from wilful misconduct or gross
    negligence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data">9. Personal data protection</h2>
  <p>
    The processing of personal data you provide through the Site is governed by our{' '}
    <a href={localizedPath('privacy', locale)}>Privacy Policy</a>, which forms an integral part of
    these Terms and complies with Law No. 29733, the Peruvian Personal Data Protection Law, and its
    Regulations approved by Supreme Decree No. 016-2024-JUS.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    {site.shortName} may amend these Terms to reflect regulatory, technical or service changes. The
    version in force is always the one published on this page, showing its last updated date.
    Continued use of the Site after a new version is published constitutes acceptance of it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">11. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Peru. For any dispute arising from their
    interpretation or performance, the parties submit to the courts of the Judicial District of
    Lima, waiving the jurisdiction of their own domicile, without prejudice to the rights granted to
    users by consumer protection legislation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about these Terms, write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email.legal}`}>{site.email.legal}</a> or to the postal address given in
    section 1.
  </p>
</Legal>
